{%- comment -%}
  LOCAL OVERRIDE of al_folio_core's `_includes/footer.liquid`.
  Rebuilt to DESIGN.md §7: logo + copyright on the left, two small labelled link
  groups on the right, separated from the page by a hairline top border.

  Upstream branches on `site.footer_fixed` to pin the footer to the viewport.
  DESIGN.md has no fixed footer, so that branch is gone and `_config.yml` sets
  `footer_fixed: false` to keep the two in agreement.

  The right-hand links read `_data/socials.yml`, which still holds al-folio's
  demo values (Einstein). They will come good on their own once S0.2/S0.4
  replaces that data — nothing here needs editing for that.
{%- endcomment -%}

<footer class="site-footer" role="contentinfo">
  {%- if site.newsletter.enabled -%}
    {%- if site.plugins contains 'al_newsletter' -%}
      {% include plugins/al_newsletter_form_center.liquid %}
    {%- else -%}
      {% include newsletter.liquid %}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="site-footer__inner">
    <div class="site-footer__brand">
      <a class="site-logo" href="{{ '/' | relative_url }}">
        <span class="site-logo__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="site-logo__name">
          {%- if site.title == 'blank' -%}
            {{- site.first_name }}
            {{ site.last_name -}}
          {%- else -%}
            {{- site.title -}}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      </a>
      {%- comment -%}
        Upstream's credit line, kept deliberately. DESIGN.md §7 shows only
        "© 2026 · built with jekyll", but dropping the Jekyll / al-folio /
        GitHub Pages attribution would quietly strip credit the project is owed.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="site-footer__meta">
        &copy; Copyright {{ site.time | date: '%Y' }}
        {{ site.first_name }}
        {{ site.middle_name }}
        {{ site.last_name }}.
        {{ site.footer_text }}
        {%- if site.last_updated %} Last updated: {{ 'now' | date: '%B %d, %Y' }}.{% endif -%}
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      DESIGN.md §7 draws two labelled text groups here ("contact" / "follow").
      Replaced with an icon row by request.

      This is an explicit list, not `{% social_links %}`, because the footer and
      the about page want different sets: the about page shows everything in
      `_data/socials.yml` (CV, RSS, and whatever else is configured), while the
      footer is only "how to reach me". Values still come from socials.yml, so
      there is one place to change an address — but adding a service there does
      NOT add it here, which is the intent. Add a block below to include one.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <nav class="site-footer__socials" aria-label="Contact">
      {%- comment -%}
        Four links, most-important first: email is the author's stated best way
        to be reached, then the two profiles, then the feed.

        Left out on purpose, and both still present on the about page:
          - CV      duplicates LinkedIn, and gets its own page at M2-S2.7
          - Scholar one paper; publications gets its own page at M2-S2.5
        The footer repeats on every page, so a weak link gets the site's heaviest
        repetition — which is the argument for keeping this list short.
      {%- endcomment -%}

      {%- if site.data.socials.email -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Hand-built rather than `{% al_email_protect_link %}`, which renders the
          address as text ("user [at] host") and would replace the icon. The
          plugin's JS is delegated and only reads `data-eu` / `data-ed` off
          `.al-email-protect`, leaving any children alone — including this icon.
          Splitting here means the built HTML never contains the joined address,
          which is the point: harvesters parse markup, they do not run JS.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign email_parts = site.data.socials.email | split: '@' -%}
        {%- if site.protect_email and email_parts.size == 2 -%}
          <a
            href="#"
            class="al-email-protect"
            data-eu="{{ email_parts[0] }}"
            data-ed="{{ email_parts[1] }}"
            title="Email (click to copy)"
            aria-label="Copy email address"
          >
            <i class="fa-solid fa-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </a>
        {%- else -%}
          <a href="mailto:{{ site.data.socials.email }}" title="Email" aria-label="Email">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if site.data.socials.github_username -%}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/{{ site.data.socials.github_username }}"
          title="GitHub"
          aria-label="GitHub"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          <i class="fa-brands fa-github" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if site.data.socials.linkedin_username -%}
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/{{ site.data.socials.linkedin_username }}"
          title="LinkedIn"
          aria-label="LinkedIn"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          <i class="fa-brands fa-linkedin" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

      <a href="{{ '/feed.xml' | relative_url }}" title="RSS feed" aria-label="RSS feed">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-square-rss" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </div>

  {%- if site.impressum_path -%}
    <p class="site-footer__meta site-footer__impressum">
      <a href="{{ site.impressum_path | relative_url }}">Impressum</a>
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}
</footer>
